  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>tr_dim_date - generates mart_dim_date, one row for every day of 2003 to 2005.
Connection: MySQL:sampledata (localhost, pentaho_admin).
Run dim_date.sql first: it creates the table.

1. gr-days: Generate Rows, limit 1096, start_date = 2003-01-01.
2. seq-day_offset: Add sequence, day_offset from 0, by 1.
3. calc-date_parts: Calculator, the_date = start_date + day_offset days, its year,
   quarter, month and day parts, and date_key = year * 10000 + month * 100 + day.
4. vm-quarter_name: Value mapper, 1 to 4 become QTR1 to QTR4.
5. vm-month_name: Value mapper, 1 to 12 become Jan to Dec.
6. sv-drop_helpers: Select values, removes start_date and day_offset.
7. to-dim_date: Table output to mart_dim_date, truncated first.

Shipped data: 1,096 rows, from 20030101 to 20051231.</note>
      <xloc>96</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>496</width>
      <heigth>260</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
